# HAL shared-code sync manifest
# ─────────────────────────────
# These 5 files are VENDORED from bz5_recon (upstream owns them). They are
# copied verbatim except the package line + a checksum header. DO NOT edit
# their bodies in companion — re-sync from recon when divergence is needed
# (see DECODER_CHANGELOG.md for the decoder delta process).
#
# v0.1.29+107: a 6th vendored file (Bz3TelemetrySubscriber.kt) joins them.
# It comes from a DIFFERENT recon version (p100 / v0.10.79) than the original
# five (p078), so the manifest now supports a PER-LINE version after the SHA:
#     <file>.kt  <sha64>  [version string]
# A line without a trailing version uses the manifest-wide `version:` default.
#
# tools/hal_sync_check.py reads this manifest:
#   - if a listed file is ABSENT from this dir → WARN (not yet vendored)
#   - if PRESENT → its checksum header must declare its line's version + SHA
#
# Vendoring procedure (do once, on the Mac that has both repos):
#   for each file below:
#     cp  bz5-recon/android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/bz5/recon/live/<F>  ./<F>
#     set first line:  package com.bz5companion.bz5_companion.hal
#     paste header above package:
#       // === SHARED FROM bz5_recon ===
#       // Source: bz5-recon/.../live/<F>
#       // Synced: 2026-06-10 (recon v0.10.57, commit p078)
#       // SHA256: <SHA from this manifest>
#       // DO NOT EDIT directly — re-sync from source repo when divergence needed.
#
# Target package (companion): com.bz5companion.bz5_companion.hal
# (handoff suggested com.bz5.companion.hal; we keep the module's existing
#  root for consistency with the rest of android/.../bz5_companion/)

